# What the site build does not need.
#
# The deploy runs from the repo root, because fusion/site is a workspace package and
# its dependencies are built from source. That would otherwise upload a great
# deal the build has no use for.
#
# No `docs/` pattern, and none with a leading slash either: `docs/` is a
# gitignore-style pattern that would match `cortex/docs` and `helix/docs`,
# which are workspace members, and `fusion/docs/insights` is
# `@fusion.dev/insights`, which the site depends on. Excluding any of them
# breaks `bun install` before the build starts.

# Build output and scratch, rebuilt on Vercel anyway.
#
# **`.next-dev` is named separately, and `**/.next/` does not cover it.** The
# site builds development into its own directory so that a turbo task writing
# `.next` cannot pull the floor out from under a running `next dev` (the reason
# is in `next.config.ts`), and that directory is the largest thing in the
# repository by an order of magnitude: measured at 23GB across 9,903 files,
# because a dev server's output accumulates rather than replacing itself.
#
# Git never sees it, `.gitignore` having excluded it since it was introduced, so
# the omission here was invisible until a deploy tried to upload it. What that
# looks like is `Upload aborted` three times over and then the CLI killed
# outright, which reads as a network fault and is not one.
.claude/
.local/
target/
**/.next/
**/.next-dev/
**/.turbo/
**/dist/
**/node_modules/

# Rust, which nothing in this project builds.
Cargo.lock
Cargo.toml
